# Prompt
Imports:
import ParsedSviDirectory from "./sviParser/parsedSviDirectory";
import { SVIFile, SviFileToLoad } from "./types";

Please create a class performing checks on correctness of all the *.svi files in the project.
Input - a list of full paths to SVI files.
A list of checks:
* Check 1: If several *.svi files have the same destination file (target path after 
resolution)
Then output error about it.
When performing this check, please ignore items with SviFileToLoad.isPreliminary = true
as they can contain duplicated items, but it's okay.
Output format example:
-------
Error: Multiple SVI files are configured to generate the same destination file: 'C:\temp\test.js':
- C:\temp\test.svi
- C:\temp\test2.svi
----
The error is critical because a file can be overwritten. With a big probability,
it can happen due to a human error

* Check 2: If *.svi file in the # Destination points to itself (destination filename
equals to the file name itself including *.svi extension).
When comparing, use relative path for svi file and destination file to be sure 
that the comparison is correct.

The error message:
Error in file <path_to_svi_file>: The destination file cannot be the same as the source file. Please change the destination file and try again.

* Check 3: If *.svi file in the # Destination contains more than one line
with text separated by a line feed (/n)
(empty lines please don't consider)

The error message:
Error in file <path_to_svi_file>: More than one item in the # Destination section